<title><%= content_for(:title) || "Playverto Verto Studio" %></title>
<%# interactive-widget: for the player, and now the editor too. On
    Chrome/Android it makes the soft keyboard shrink the LAYOUT viewport, so a
    `position: fixed; inset: 0` overlay becomes genuinely the visible area and
    its footer rides above the keyboard instead of being stranded mid-screen.
    The editor earns it because the mobile studio makes the cards feed exactly
    such an overlay (mobile_studio_controller adds .preview-overlay at ≤767px)
    and a creator types INTO that card — the same problem, the same fix.
    Still off elsewhere: the auth pages depend on the browser's ordinary
    scroll-the-field-into-view behaviour. iOS Safari ignores the hint entirely
    — see lib/viewport_height.js, which is what carries that platform. %>
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1,viewport-fit=cover<%= ",interactive-widget=resizes-content" if controller_name == "player" || @interactive_widget_resize %>">
<meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
<meta name="mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
<%# A second theme-color meta wouldn't win — browsers honour the first valid
    one, so a per-Verto colour has to replace this tag, not follow it. %>
<meta name="theme-color" content="<%= content_for(:theme_color) || "#1C2034" %>">
<meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style" content="black-translucent">
<%= csrf_meta_tags %>
<%= csp_meta_tag %>

<%= yield :head %>

<%# @pwa_manifest_url (PlayerController#show) swaps in the per-Verto
    manifest so "Add to Home Screen" installs the Verto itself, scoped to
    /play/, instead of the studio-wide one every other page keeps. %>
<link rel="manifest" href="<%= @pwa_manifest_url || pwa_manifest_path %>">
<%= favicon_link_tag "favicon.svg", type: "image/svg+xml" %>
<%= favicon_link_tag "favicon.svg", rel: "apple-touch-icon", type: "image/svg+xml" %>
<%# ABeeZee/Alata are now self-hosted (app/assets/tailwind/application.css +
    public/fonts/) instead of loaded from Google's fonts.googleapis.com /
    fonts.gstatic.com CDN, which sent every visitor's IP address to Google
    before any consent — see the @font-face rules for details. They ship as
    part of the "tailwind" stylesheet below, so no separate <link> is needed. %>
<%= stylesheet_link_tag "tailwind", "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
<%= stylesheet_link_tag "application", "data-turbo-track": "reload" %>
<%= render "layouts/i18n_js" %>
<%= javascript_importmap_tags %>
<%# The player's interactive modules, fetched WITH the page instead of after
    it. Controllers are pinned preload: false and lazy-loaded (right for the
    dashboard, where 60+ files up front dominated first paint) — but on /play
    that lazy chain is a four-deep waterfall (application → controllers/index
    → each controller → its lib imports), and on a cold cache over venue wifi
    the respondent had a painted, dead card for the duration: "having to
    refresh the page to be able to select an answer" — the refresh worked
    because the second load hit warm caches. These hints flatten the chain to
    one parallel wave; the lazy loader then resolves instantly from the module
    map. Scoped to the player (and the owner's chromeless preview of it) so
    every other page keeps the deliberate lazy behaviour. %>
<% if controller_name == "player" || @chromeless %>
  <%= javascript_module_preload_tag(*player_module_preload_paths) %>
<% end %>
